decisions:
  - id: d-1
    decision: Full B (a) contracts-only over team-recommended B-lite synthesis
    rationale: User picked completeness framing after team (architect/Jinx/Helix/Loid) recommended cutting marketplace primitives; user override accepted with documented migration risk on bundle metadata.
  - id: d-2
    decision: Object-shape partners (Loid) over string[] (Architect)
    rationale: Object array `[{id, relation?, share_notebooks?}]` is durable for v6.1 learning-loop knob; string[] would force migration.
  - id: d-3
    decision: Asymmetric pairings as `pending` status, not warn
    rationale: Loid's framing — one-way is legal and mirrors nevr.land trust contract semantics; warn-only would train users to ignore.
  - id: d-4
    decision: Pair notebook namespace reserved at `_pairs/{a-b}/`, not wired to learning yet
    rationale: Path helper only at v6.0.3; reserves the surface so v6.1+ pair-learning doesn't force a schema migration.
  - id: d-5
    decision: Failure Ledger primitive PUNTED to v6.1
    rationale: User chose to ship lore-rejection telemetry first and design the ledger from real data.
  - id: d-6
    decision: Nora's broken v5.37.4 registration fixed by manually constructing `~/.paradigm/agents/ftux.agent`
    rationale: agents.yaml/adoptions/roster entries existed but global .agent profile was never published; reconstructed from the agents.yaml entry.
learnings:
  - 'Builder agent hit Edit/Write permission denial mid-session; recovery was straightforward when I executed the builder''s full plan myself (had the orientation captured in their report). Future: for substantive multi-file builds, verify builder has write permissions before delegating.'
  - Orchestrate_inline auto-planner ignored explicit `agents` override (kept architect, dropped advocate/dx/forge); workaround was launching the 4 design agents directly via Task tool with parallel run_in_background. Auto-planner's agent selection appears keyword-triggered, not override-respecting.
  - 'ftux/Nora was a partial-registration: agents.yaml + adoptions + roster entries existed but no global .agent profile file. `paradigm_agent_activate` requires the .agent profile, not just registration entries. Ship-completion check should verify the .agent file exists for any new core agent.'
  - Per-pair notebook namespace pattern (`_pairs/{alphabetically-canonical-id-pair}/`) is the right shape for partner state — stays out of either agent's profile, canonical regardless of who declares the pair, leaves room for v6.1 learning without schema changes.
  - Architect's plan correctly flagged that AgentProfile is duplicated in `agent/index.ts` (deliberate to avoid cross-package import); editing the schema requires updating BOTH the canonical paradigm-mcp type AND the local CLI duplicate.
